% The forms a negated literal takes.  A negated literal binds nothing, so it
% is tested wherever its variables are bound, however it is written: before
% the literal that binds them, over a relation of arity zero, with constants
% for arguments, or in a query.
item(pen).
item(ink).
item(pad).
sold(ink).
closed.

% Written before the literal that binds X.
unsold(X) :- not sold(X), item(X).

% Arity zero: closed/0 holds, so nothing is open.
open(X) :- item(X), not closed.

% Constants only: holds for every item, because nothing sold a pad.
stocked(X) :- item(X), not sold(pad).

unsold(X)?
open(X)?
stocked(X)?
not sold(pen)?
item(X), not unsold(X)?
not sold(ink)?
